HST Office: equation previews in more fonts and in EMF.
- EMF previews (MathType 7, ChemDraw): text in legacy Vietnamese fonts (TCVN3 ".VnTime", VNI
  "VNI-Times") is decoded and drawn with Times New Roman/Arial, as WMF previews already are
  (EXTTEXTOUTA bytes; EXTTEXTOUTW keeps the byte codes as U+00xx/U+F0xx/Windows-1252).
- Old MathType equations use the Euclid fonts: "Euclid Math One" (script), "Euclid Math Two"
  (double-struck), "Euclid Fraktur" letters become Unicode mathematical letters drawn with
  the bundled DejaVu Math TeX Gyre; "Euclid Symbol" / "Euclid Extra" have the Symbol / MT Extra
  layout and use their handling; "Euclid" (the text font) is drawn as Times New Roman.
  Letter mapping: Unicode Mathematical Alphanumeric Symbols; the Math Two relations follow the
  transpect fontmaps (BSD-2-Clause).

